    {
      "id": "text-271",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3020,
      "width": 1763.3000000000002,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2146049,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 28381559,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reference: briareus-windows. Other clients match this structure, differing only as noted here.\nDatabase pool rows show the label (or host:port) over host:port. The section title carries '· N sessions', the pool's capacity. Delete reads 'Remove this server from the pool' and asks 'Remove <name> from the pool?'.\nPort is a narrow cell (140px) beside Host. Username and Password share the row equally.\nThe SSH Database tab is offered only when the server's catalog has GET /settings/ssh/servers/{id}/db-credentials. Otherwise that tab explains the server must be updated.\nForge account has Save and 🗑 only (no clone). A row's dot means a token is stored.\nA tab with unsaved changes gets ' •' (for example 'SSH server •', 'Forge account •'). New entries show as 'New database server' / 'New SSH server' / 'New Forge account' with 'not saved yet' in the sidebar, and only Save in the\nheader.\nRegion names (sidebar, canvas, raise, sunken) are the theme.* roles; widths and margins are layout.* in tokens/. Greys only, on purpose.",
      "originalText": "Reference: briareus-windows. Other clients match this structure, differing only as noted here.\nDatabase pool rows show the label (or host:port) over host:port. The section title carries '· N sessions', the pool's capacity. Delete reads 'Remove this server from the pool' and asks 'Remove <name> from the pool?'.\nPort is a narrow cell (140px) beside Host. Username and Password share the row equally.\nThe SSH Database tab is offered only when the server's catalog has GET /settings/ssh/servers/{id}/db-credentials. Otherwise that tab explains the server must be updated.\nForge account has Save and 🗑 only (no clone). A row's dot means a token is stored.\nA tab with unsaved changes gets ' •' (for example 'SSH server •', 'Forge account •'). New entries show as 'New database server' / 'New SSH server' / 'New Forge account' with 'not saved yet' in the sidebar, and only Save in the\nheader.\nRegion names (sidebar, canvas, raise, sunken) are the theme.* roles; widths and margins are layout.* in tokens/. Greys only, on purpose.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    }
  ],
